   "he": "הָאִשָּׁה אֶת בְּנָהּ וְכוּ׳. הָא תּוּ לְמָה לִי? הָא תְּנָא לֵיהּ רֵישָׁא: הָאִישׁ אֶת אִמּוֹ, וְהָאִישׁ אֶת אִשְׁתּוֹ!",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches that «a woman» bequeaths to «her son,» her husband, and her maternal uncles, but she does not inherit from them. The Gemara asks: «Why do I» need «this as well? But it is» already «taught» in «the former clause: A man» inherits from «his mother and a man» inherits from «his wife.» The halakha stated in this clause seems to be the same as that of the other clause."
  }
